/** Keyed by the same 60 slugs: 100–125 words on this element-animal at work and in close relationships, specific to the combination. */
export const ELEMENT_ANIMAL_LIFE: Record<string, string> = {
  "wood-rat": "In an office, the Wood Rat is the colleague who has already sketched three ways to grow a side project nobody else noticed. Readings place this combination in fundraising, product development, community organising and editorial planning, where scouting resources and introducing the right people both count. A shared calendar and one trusted colleague who asks which idea comes first help it stay on course. At home, the Wood Rat usually shows care through logistics: tables booked, birthdays remembered, a savings pot quietly growing for the next trip. In return it hopes for someone who appreciates the forethought and shares its optimism. Trouble tends to start when it overcommits the household's evenings and weekends, then lies awake fretting that everything is slipping.",
  "fire-rat": "Give a Fire Rat a negotiation and it often comes alive. This version of the sign pairs a calculating mind with a theatrical streak, so pitching, trading, campaign strategy, journalism and live events are frequently named as natural ground. Colleagues admire the speed and occasionally wince at the bluntness, which is why a cooling-off rule before sending a sharp email saves a great deal of goodwill. Romantically, the Fire Rat is attentive and flirtatious, keen to impress with clever gifts and last-minute plans. It wants someone who can trade banter without taking every quip to heart. The familiar flashpoint is jealousy laced with worry: when it senses a threat to security, sparks fly quickly and the apology arrives rather more slowly.",
  "earth-rat": "Spreadsheets, contracts and long-range budgets suit the Earth Rat unusually well. Classic descriptions show a careful operator who would rather build a dependable system than chase a quick win, which points towards accountancy, property, procurement, logistics and operations management. A manager who explains the reasoning behind decisions earns its loyalty far faster than one relying on charm. Closer to home, this Rat offers ballast: bills settled on time, a well-stocked cupboard, a plan for the years ahead. It looks for a companion who values that steadiness and does not mistake caution for dullness. Tension usually builds when security drifts into control, and whoever shares the household starts to suspect every small purchase is being audited.",
  "metal-rat": "The Metal Rat often treats a career like a campaign, complete with targets, milestones and a clear-eyed view of the competition. Traditional accounts match it with finance, law, consultancy, engineering management and any setting where sharp analysis must end in a firm recommendation. Autonomy and measurable goals bring out its best; vague leadership irritates it. As a partner it is protective and exacting, determined to secure a comfortable future for the people it loves. Ideally it pairs with someone who has ambitions of their own and the nerve to disagree out loud. The rub is inflexibility: a Metal Rat may defend its plan long after circumstances have changed, leaving the other person feeling overruled rather than consulted.",
  "water-rat": "Counselling, diplomacy, recruitment, investigative writing and market intelligence are fields often linked with the Water Rat, because it picks up moods and hidden motives almost by reflex. It gathers information quietly and usually knows who really holds influence in a meeting long before the organisation chart admits it. A clear brief and written deadlines keep that perceptiveness pointed at results rather than gossip. Among family and close friends, the Water Rat is tender, adaptable and a superb confidant, the sort who notices a change of tone in a two-word message. It craves emotional candour and a partner who will not confuse tact with evasion. The usual snag is avoidance: smoothing over a disagreement to keep the peace, so the issue resurfaces later carrying extra weight.",
  "wood-ox": "A Wood Ox brings stamina to collaborative work, the sort of person who stays after the meeting to finish the shared document properly. Teaching, agriculture, architecture, public service and running small charities are the usual suggestions, since each rewards patient building alongside other people. It copes best when its steady contribution is acknowledged and when change is announced early rather than sprung on it. In partnership the Wood Ox is dependable and rather more openly affectionate than most Oxen, happy to tend a vegetable patch, cook for friends or fix the dripping tap without being asked. It needs someone who notices these quiet efforts. Friction arrives when it shoulders everybody's burdens without complaint, then hits a stubborn, silent limit that nobody saw coming.",
  "fire-ox": "Put a Fire Ox in charge of a stalled project and things generally start moving. This combination joins the Ox's endurance to a commanding presence, so readings connect it with construction, manufacturing, sports coaching, emergency planning and senior management. It respects hierarchy and expects equal commitment from colleagues, which works well once expectations are spelled out in writing. Privately, a Fire Ox is fiercely loyal and shows love through provision and protection, often far more passionately than the Ox's reserved reputation suggests. Respect matters enormously to it, as does a partner willing to stand their ground. The recurring problem is force: when a disagreement drags on, the Fire Ox may simply push harder, and the other person feels flattened rather than heard.",
  "earth-ox": "The Earth Ox is the craftsperson of the zodiac, content to spend years perfecting a skill that others would drop after a season. Banking, civil engineering, farming, archiving, joinery and quality control are frequently mentioned, since each prizes accuracy over flair. Clear processes, fair pay and a boss who keeps promises suit it; office politics simply bore it. In a long partnership the Earth Ox offers constancy measured in decades rather than gestures, from the same anniversary restaurant to the car serviced before every holiday. Honesty, routine and a settled home are what it asks in return. Loved ones sometimes wish for more spoken warmth, and the old sticking point is rigidity, especially when plans change at short notice.",
  "metal-ox": "Few combinations are pictured as more relentless at work than the Metal Ox. It sets exacting standards, follows procedure to the letter and tends to excel in auditing, heavy industry, structural engineering, compliance and senior administration. Clear lines of authority and the freedom to finish a job properly suit it, whereas constant reorganisation grates. Within a marriage or long friendship it is principled and utterly reliable, keeping every promise it makes however inconvenient. What it seeks is somebody who prizes integrity and does not need constant flattery. The weak point is severity: a Metal Ox can judge a loved one's untidy habits or emotional outbursts harshly, and compromise may feel to it like quietly lowering the bar.",
  "water-ox": "Among Oxen, the Water version is usually pictured as the quiet strategist who sees problems coming before anyone else. Planning, mediation, environmental management, records work and patient technical roles where judgement outranks speed are typical suggestions. It listens carefully in meetings, speaks last and is often right, so colleagues learn to ask for its view before deciding. With a partner, the Water Ox offers calm attentiveness and a gentler patience than its siblings, plus a surprising knack for knowing when to leave someone be. It needs a companion who can coax feelings out without pressure. The common difficulty is reserve: worries are stored away, and a loved one may discover them only after the Water Ox has settled something important alone.",
  "wood-tiger": "The Wood Tiger leads by inviting people in, which makes it a natural founder of clubs, campaigns and creative studios. Readings tie it to advocacy, festival production, outdoor education, publishing and early-stage ventures, anywhere bold ideas need allies to succeed. Its enthusiasm can outrun the budget, so a grounded co-lead who handles schedules and invoices is a real asset. In romance the Wood Tiger is open-hearted and fun, eager to share expeditions and late-night conversations about how the world could be better. It wants freedom within commitment and someone happy to share it with a wide circle of friends. Where it rubs is scattered attention: so many invitations accepted that the closest relationship occasionally gets the leftovers.",
  "fire-tiger": "A Fire Tiger at work resembles a weather front: dramatic, energising and impossible to ignore. Tradition links this blend with entrepreneurship, emergency response, performance, activism and high-stakes sales, roles that reward nerve and fast decisions. Slow approval chains frustrate it badly; owning a clear mission suits it far better, and a meticulous deputy keeps the brilliance from burning out by Thursday. In love the Fire Tiger is extravagant, given to grand gestures and fierce protectiveness. Admiration and room to roam are what it asks, along with a partner secure enough not to cling. Clashes usually follow impulsiveness: a sudden decision about money, a job offer or moving house, announced over dinner rather than discussed beforehand.",
  "earth-tiger": "Courage with a plan is the Earth Tiger's signature at work. Tradition casts it as a realistic risk-taker suited to project leadership, property development, operations, policy and coaching, where boldness has to answer to budgets. Before charging it prefers to understand the whole terrain, then it commits completely. Clear objectives and a fair hearing for its proposals keep it engaged for years. Away from the job, the Earth Tiger is protective and steady, more willing than other Tigers to stay put and put down roots. It asks for trust and some independence, perhaps a hobby that is entirely its own. The usual difficulty is pride: having weighed a decision carefully, it can be slow to accept that a partner's hunch might be wiser.",
  "metal-tiger": "The Metal Tiger approaches a career like a duel: focused, competitive and determined to win cleanly. Law, competitive sport, security work, investigative journalism and turnaround management come up again and again, since each tests nerve and principle together. It performs best with a clearly defined target and minimal micromanagement, and colleagues usually admire its candour even while flinching at its bluntness. As a partner, the Metal Tiger is intensely loyal and defends the people it loves without a moment's hesitation. It wants an equal who will not be intimidated by its intensity. Conflict appears when certainty hardens into an all-or-nothing stance, turning a small disagreement about holidays or chores into a contest that somebody has to lose.",
  "water-tiger": "Tradition paints the Water Tiger as a visionary who can sense where a field is heading before the trend has a name. Design, consultancy, international work, documentary-making and teaching are commonly named, as intuition about people and patterns gives it an edge. Flexible structures and collaborators who welcome unconventional ideas suit it; without a deadline, however, it can drift. Between two people, the Water Tiger is perceptive and kind, able to read a partner's mood from across a crowded room. It needs space to think and someone who respects sudden bursts of independence. The hitch is inconsistency: warmth one week, distance the next, which can leave the other person unsure exactly where they stand.",
  "wood-rabbit": "Gentle diplomacy and an eye for beauty make the Wood Rabbit a gift to any team that must agree on something. Readings associate it with interior design, people management, horticulture, editing and arts administration, roles where taste and tact both matter. It works best in calm surroundings among colleagues who value courtesy, and loud rivalries drain it quickly. With loved ones, the Wood Rabbit is affectionate and generous, often the person who remembers favourite biscuits and arranges cosy evenings with candles and board games. It asks for reassurance and a peaceful home. Strain usually grows out of its reluctance to refuse: it agrees to too many favours, then withdraws quietly when exhausted rather than admitting it needs a rest.",
  "fire-rabbit": "The Fire Rabbit adds sparkle and persuasion to a sign known chiefly for grace. Public relations, hospitality, fashion, theatre and client-facing work are typical matches, since charm is half the job. It flourishes with visible appreciation and a pleasant, well-run workplace, while harsh criticism can wound it more deeply than it lets on. Romantically, the Fire Rabbit is warm and expressive, quick to celebrate a partner's wins with a toast or a handwritten card. Emotional reciprocity and plenty of shared fun matter greatly to it. The awkward pattern is mood: a bruised feeling can flare into a sharp remark, after which the Rabbit side retreats from confrontation and leaves the real issue only half aired.",
  "earth-rabbit": "In practical terms, the Earth Rabbit is the reliable diplomat: tactful, organised and sensible with money. Office management, conveyancing, librarianship, mediation and independent retail are frequently suggested, because steady judgement and a pleasant manner build trust there. It prefers stability, transparent processes and a desk where it can work without constant interruption. Within the family, the Earth Rabbit creates a comfortable, orderly home and rarely loses its temper. Loyalty and kept promises are what it values most, and it repays them with years of quiet devotion. The sticking point is caution bordering on inertia: it may postpone difficult conversations, house moves or career changes until the right moment has slipped past unnoticed.",
  "metal-rabbit": "The Metal Rabbit pairs refined taste with a surprising backbone. Readings suit it to curation, jewellery, legal drafting, fine printing, private banking and design direction, where high standards and discretion are prized. It likes clear rules and the chance to polish work until it is genuinely excellent, whereas sloppy deadlines and noisy open-plan floors wear it down. With a partner, the Metal Rabbit is devoted and quietly protective, though it shows feeling through considered gestures more than words. Privacy and respect for its boundaries are non-negotiable. Discord usually comes from perfectionism turned on the relationship itself: a cool, critical silence when a loved one falls short of a standard that was never actually spoken.",
  "water-rabbit": "Sensitive and imaginative, the Water Rabbit tends to shine in work that asks for empathy and creative depth. Illustration, social work, music, translation and pastoral care are all mentioned in this context. It does best in kind environments with predictable rhythms and managers who deliver feedback gently and in private. In love the Water Rabbit is tender and attuned, offering deep comfort and the sort of listening that makes a bad day feel lighter. Emotional safety matters above almost everything, along with a partner who never needs to raise their voice. Difficulty arises from absorbed moods: it may take on a partner's stress as its own, then slip into silence rather than explain what hurts.",
  "wood-dragon": "The Wood Dragon thinks in decades and enjoys rallying others behind a long undertaking. It is commonly linked with urban planning, school leadership, publishing, social enterprise and architecture, fields where a vision has to be shared before it can be built. Genuine latitude and colleagues who can translate big sketches into budgets suit it well. Unlike some Dragons, it usually credits the team generously when things go right. In relationships, the Wood Dragon is magnanimous and inspiring, cheering a partner's ambitions as eagerly as its own. It wants admiration and a lively intellectual companion. Tension surfaces when its many schemes crowd the calendar, and a partner begins to feel like one ambitious project among several.",
  "fire-dragon": "Few signs are portrayed as more magnetic on a stage than the Fire Dragon. Politics, broadcasting, entrepreneurship, entertainment and executive leadership are the classic settings, wherever presence and conviction move people. It thrives when it can set direction and rarely enjoys answering to anyone, which makes a trusted adviser who can say no to it in private invaluable. At home the Fire Dragon is generous and theatrical in love, fond of lavish birthdays and spontaneous weekends away. Loyalty and respect for its pride are essential to it. The usual flashpoint is temper combined with dominance: a disagreement may register as a challenge to its authority, and the household starts to orbit its moods.",
  "earth-dragon": "The Earth Dragon is often pictured as a builder-king, ambitious yet patient enough to pour solid foundations. Corporate strategy, real estate, government, large-scale engineering and institution-building suit it, since vision there has to survive committees and spreadsheets. It respects competence, prefers fair procedures and earns trust by delivering exactly what it promised. In close relationships this Dragon is protective, generous and dependable, eager to provide comfort and standing for the family. It needs appreciation for the responsibility it carries, voiced rather than assumed. Friction shows up around authority: because it shoulders so much, an Earth Dragon may assume its plan for holidays, budgets or schooling should simply prevail.",
  "metal-dragon": "An iron will drives the Metal Dragon towards its goals, and tradition describes a formidable professional. Law, finance, elite sport, military command and turnaround consulting are typical associations, each prizing decisiveness and incorruptible standards. It works best given a clear mandate and full ownership of results, and shared credit can rankle. Even rivals tend to respect its honesty. In love the Metal Dragon is loyal, principled and fiercely protective of anyone it calls its own. A partner of strong character who can meet its intensity without flinching suits it best. The friction most often mentioned is inflexibility: once convinced, it rarely softens, and loved ones may feel measured against an impossible ideal.",
  "water-dragon": "The Water Dragon is usually seen as the most tactful of Dragons, ambitious yet able to read a room before making its move. International relations, consultancy, media strategy, negotiation and cross-border trade are commonly named, because there vision benefits from tact. Flexible structures and a role that lets it connect people across departments bring out its best, and colleagues often find it easier to approach than other Dragons. As a partner, the Water Dragon is perceptive and generous, alert to a loved one's shifting moods. It needs freedom to pursue large ideas and someone who shares its curiosity. Problems usually arise when it changes direction without warning, leaving everyone else scrambling to catch up.",
  "wood-snake": "Thoughtful, artistic and quietly ambitious, the Wood Snake tends to do its finest work away from the spotlight. Writing, restoration, landscape design, archives and advisory roles are its traditional territory, as depth, patience and aesthetic judgement all pay off there. It needs time to think and a workspace that feels considered. A mentor who trusts its slow-burning projects usually gets remarkable results. In love the Wood Snake is devoted and refined, fond of shared books, gardens and long, unhurried dinners. Loyalty and intellectual intimacy are what it seeks. The difficulty lies in privacy: plans and feelings are kept close, and a partner may sense that the full picture is being withheld.",
  "fire-snake": "The Fire Snake combines strategic patience with a real hunger for influence. Investigative journalism, political strategy, investment, competitive debating and leadership in cut-throat industries are frequent associations, wherever reading motives and acting at the right moment matter. It prefers control over its own agenda and grows suspicious when information is kept from it. In private, the Fire Snake is intense, seductive and devoted, lavishing attention on the person it chooses. Exclusivity and transparency are its core requirements. The usual source of conflict is possessiveness: jealousy can flare when it feels shut out, and its sharp intuition sometimes leaps to conclusions a partner never intended, especially late at night.",
  "earth-snake": "Calm under pressure and wise about money, the Earth Snake is cast as the steady counsel behind successful ventures. Accountancy, wealth management, property, estate planning and senior administration are frequently mentioned. It moves carefully, checks every clause and rarely makes the same mistake twice, so employers who reward discretion and long service tend to keep it for years. To a spouse or close friend, the Earth Snake offers composure, loyalty and practical security, plus a dry wit reserved for intimates. It wants stability and somebody who respects privacy. The common complaint from loved ones is slowness to open up: affection appears in deeds, while verbal reassurance can feel rationed.",
  "metal-snake": "Precision and self-possession define the Metal Snake at work. Cybersecurity, forensic accounting, luxury goods, legal analysis and strategic planning are linked with it, fields that reward discretion, polish and unwavering focus. Autonomy, high standards and a long runway for ambitious goals suit it, and it can outwork almost anyone once the objective is clear. In relationships the Metal Snake chooses carefully and then commits deeply, offering steadfast loyalty in exchange for trust. It needs a partner with self-respect and a life of their own. Trouble generally stems from its cool reserve and occasional suspicion: it may quietly test a loved one's loyalty instead of simply asking a direct question.",
  "water-snake": "The Water Snake is traditionally portrayed as a perceptive analyst who sees beneath surfaces. Intelligence analysis, editing, counselling, archival work and long-range planning all appear in readings, since insight into people and patterns makes a difference. Usually it works quietly and delivers conclusions others missed, and a trusted environment with few interruptions brings out its best. In close bonds the Water Snake is intuitive and soothing, able to sense a partner's needs before they are spoken. It hopes for emotional depth and discretion in return. The typical friction is secrecy: it processes feelings privately for so long that a partner may feel excluded from decisions about their shared life.",
  "wood-horse": "Sociable and principled, the Wood Horse brings momentum to teams that need someone to get things going. Tourism, outdoor education, journalism, campaigning and travelling sales are often suggested, since variety and cooperation are both rewarded there. It flourishes with a flexible schedule and colleagues who enjoy its enthusiasm, whereas rigid desk hours dampen it quickly. In love, the Wood Horse is cheerful, generous and keen on shared adventures, from road trips to learning a new dance together. It needs freedom and a partner who joins in rather than holds back. Friction comes when its appetite for variety looks like restlessness, and a partner wonders whether settled routines will ever appeal.",
  "fire-horse": "The Fire Horse is traditionally pictured as the most spirited Horse of all, a gallop rather than a trot. Performing arts, expedition work, entrepreneurship, sport and fast-moving media are its classic arenas, since courage and showmanship pay off there. It resists close supervision and does best with ambitious targets and freedom over method. In close relationships, the Fire Horse is passionate, adventurous and honest to the point of bluntness. It needs excitement and a partner confident enough not to feel threatened by its independence. The familiar strain is volatility: it may chafe against commitments that feel limiting and act on impulse, booking the flight or quitting the job, before talking it through.",
  "earth-horse": "With an Earth stem, the Horse's energy acquires a sense of direction and a healthy respect for planning. Logistics, project management, hospitality operations, agriculture and field sales are suggested, as stamina and good sense combine in each. It still needs movement and variety, yet it is more willing than other Horses to see a long project through to the end. Fair managers and clear milestones keep it content. In relationships, the Earth Horse is warm, considerate and comparatively settled, keen to build a home base from which to set off on adventures. It needs trust and gentle encouragement. Indecision is the usual sore point: weighing too many options for travel, jobs or moves can leave a partner waiting.",
  "metal-horse": "Independent and determined, the Metal Horse wants to steer its own course at work. Freelancing, competitive sport, engineering, investment and business ownership are typical fits, because self-direction and stamina count for a great deal. It sets ambitious goals and dislikes interference, so a manager who defines outcomes and then steps back usually gets its best effort. In love, the Metal Horse is ardent and loyal on its own terms, drawn to strong-willed partners who keep their own interests. It needs independence within the relationship and straight talk. The usual friction is stubbornness: it may decide alone and then defend the decision, and the other person can feel that togetherness is negotiable rather than given.",
  "water-horse": "The Water Horse is often described as quick, adaptable and gifted with words. Communications, travel writing, diplomacy, digital media and sales are frequently named, since reading audiences and changing course nimbly matter in all of them. It thrives on variety and may lose interest in roles that repeat the same day endlessly, so a mix of projects and short deadlines keeps it focused. In relationships, the Water Horse is charming, attentive and fun, quick to sense when a partner needs cheering up. It needs novelty and lively conversation. Inconstancy causes most of the trouble: plans, enthusiasms and even opinions can shift quickly, and a partner may crave a little more predictability.",
  "wood-goat": "Kind, artistic and cooperative, the Wood Goat tends to flourish where empathy is part of the job description. Early-years teaching, craft design, community arts, gardening and charity work are commonly associated with it, since gentle persistence creates value in each. A supportive manager, a harmonious team and a little creative licence keep it content, while competitive bonus cultures usually unsettle it. In close relationships the Wood Goat is affectionate, generous and devoted to making home feel welcoming, often with fresh flowers and something baking. It wants security and appreciation. People-pleasing is the quiet hazard: it may agree to arrangements it secretly dislikes, then feel hurt that its partner never guessed.",
  "fire-goat": "The Fire Goat brings flair and unexpected courage to a sign usually known for gentleness. Performance, fashion, visual arts, events and creative direction suit it, since expressive talent there can be seen and celebrated. It works best with encouragement and a clear brief, and it may lose heart in environments that dismiss its ideas out of hand. In love, the Fire Goat is romantic, warm and dramatic, drawn to grand gestures and memorable dates. It needs reassurance and admiration as well as a stable home to return to. The usual friction is emotional weather: sudden moods, hurt feelings and impulsive spending, especially when it feels insecure about where the relationship is heading.",
  "earth-goat": "Grounded and caring, the Earth Goat tends to be regarded as the most dependable Goat in the workplace. Administration, social care, catering, horticulture and craft businesses are frequently suggested, because patience and attention to others' needs keep those settings running. It likes routines, kind colleagues and visible thanks for its effort, and it rarely complains about the unglamorous jobs. At home the Earth Goat is loyal, nurturing and practical, usually the one making sure everyone has eaten and the spare room is ready. Security matters to it, and so does a partner who notices quiet effort. Friction comes from worry: it may fret about money or the future and need more reassurance than a partner expects.",
  "metal-goat": "With a Metal stem, the Goat's creativity gains structure and resolve. Fine art, architecture, jewellery, editing and design management come up often, since refined taste and high standards are prized there. Its best output comes with clear expectations, time to perfect details and a calm studio, and unexpected changes of plan can unsettle it for days. In relationships, the Metal Goat is devoted and protective of its inner circle, though more guarded than other Goats at first. It needs loyalty and a peaceful, beautiful home. The typical friction is sensitivity to criticism: a passing remark may wound deeply and be remembered long after the other person has forgotten saying it.",
  "water-goat": "Intuitive, gentle and adaptable, the Water Goat often thrives in quiet supporting roles. Counselling, music, illustration, libraries and charity work fit it well, because empathy and imagination help others there. It does best with a supportive network and a clear structure that spares it from constant decision-making. In love, the Water Goat is tender, accommodating and quick to sense moods, often the first to notice when a partner is tired or low. It needs emotional safety and steady reassurance. Dependence and indecision are where things wobble: it may lean on a partner for every choice, or drift with the current instead of stating what it actually wants.",
  "wood-monkey": "The Wood Monkey is the inventor who also wants everyone to enjoy the workshop. Product design, science communication, educational games, software and collaborative engineering are its natural playgrounds, anywhere ingenuity and teamwork meet. It needs puzzles, a long leash and colleagues who laugh at its jokes. Routine reporting bores it, so pairing with a methodical organiser keeps good ideas from evaporating. In relationships, the Wood Monkey is playful, curious and generous with its time, always proposing a new recipe, route or project. It wants a partner who is lively company and open to experiments. Friction arises from distraction: several home projects started at once can leave half-painted walls and promises waiting.",
  "fire-monkey": "Bold, clever and competitive, the Fire Monkey enjoys being the sharpest strategist in the building. Entrepreneurship, trading, comedy, marketing and technology leadership are frequent associations, since quick thinking and showmanship win attention there. It needs a challenge big enough to hold its interest and the freedom to improvise when the plan stalls. Routine admin, left unchecked, tends to pile up on its desk. In love, the Fire Monkey is exciting, flirtatious and generous, keen on surprise trips and elaborate jokes. It needs stimulation and admiration. The familiar friction is a competitive streak that follows it home: it may treat arguments like a game to win, and a partner can feel outmanoeuvred rather than understood.",
  "earth-monkey": "The Earth Monkey channels the sign's ingenuity into practical, reliable results. Engineering, consultancy, technical teaching, logistics and small-business management are commonly named, because clever fixes have to work in the real world there. It enjoys solving genuine problems for actual clients and tends to earn trust by being both inventive and dependable. In relationships, the Earth Monkey is warm, loyal and helpful, often the friend who arrives with a toolbox and stays for supper. It needs respect for its competence and a companion who values steadiness. Friction comes from pride in being right: it may correct a partner's approach to a task rather than letting them learn their own way.",
  "metal-monkey": "With Metal as both year element and fixed element, the Metal Monkey's cleverness gains discipline and ambition. Finance, law, engineering, competitive business and technical leadership are typical fits, since sharp analysis must produce results there. It sets demanding targets, works independently and can grow impatient with colleagues who need things explained twice. In love, the Metal Monkey is passionate and loyal once committed, though selective about whom it trusts and slow to reveal vulnerability. It needs intellectual equality and honesty. Self-reliance is the catch: it may solve problems alone and present the solution as finished, leaving a partner feeling like a spectator in decisions that affect both of them.",
  "water-monkey": "The Water Monkey is often described as an intuitive, persuasive communicator. Diplomacy, writing, advertising, negotiation and talent scouting are associated with it, because reading people quickly gives it an edge. It adapts its approach on the fly and can sell an idea to a sceptical room. Varied projects and the freedom to move between teams keep it engaged, whereas a narrow role invites boredom and mischief. In relationships, the Water Monkey is charming, empathetic and entertaining, the life of most dinner parties. It looks for someone who appreciates its humour and complexity. The usual friction is evasiveness: it may deflect difficult topics with a joke, and a partner can wonder what it really feels.",
  "wood-rooster": "Organised and idealistic, the Wood Rooster likes to make systems fairer as well as tidier. Public administration, teaching, editing, event planning and charity governance are often suggested, as precision and social conscience combine in each. It needs clear goals, a team willing to keep standards high and acknowledgement of the effort it pours into detail. In love, the Wood Rooster is loyal, attentive and generous with practical help, from proofreading a partner's application to planning a holiday down to the train times. It wants appreciation and shared values. Friction comes from its exacting eye: it may notice every small flaw in shared plans and point them out before praising anything.",
  "fire-rooster": "The Fire Rooster loves to be seen doing excellent work. Broadcasting, fashion, management, event direction and public speaking suit it, since confidence and precision both shine there. It sets high standards for itself and others and tends to take charge naturally, especially when a project is visibly floundering. Recognition, an audience and a well-polished result are its favourite rewards. In love, the Fire Rooster is passionate, proud and protective, keen to show off a partner as much as itself. It needs admiration and loyalty. Friction comes from bluntness and pride: it may criticise sharply in the heat of the moment and then find an apology unusually difficult to deliver.",
  "earth-rooster": "Meticulous and reliable, the Earth Rooster brings superb organisation to any workplace. Accountancy, audit, administration, logistics and quality assurance are typical matches, since rigour and consistency matter most there. It thrives with clear procedures, an orderly desk and rewards for accuracy, and it tends to be the person who catches the error everyone else missed. In love, the Earth Rooster is steady, responsible and practical, keeping the household's paperwork in immaculate order. It needs order and fairness. Perfectionism is the pressure point: it may expect a partner to meet the same exacting standards about tidiness, budgets or schedules, and voice disappointment when they do not.",
  "metal-rooster": "Since the Rooster's fixed element is Metal, the Metal Rooster is pictured as precision distilled. Law, audit, engineering, military service and editorial standards are its traditional fields, because getting things exactly right is the whole point there. It is relentless about doing things properly, dislikes shortcuts and will happily redo work that others would call finished. In love, it is loyal and honest, sometimes to a fault, and it keeps every promise it makes. It needs respect and plain dealing in return. Friction arises from rigid judgement and a taste for argument: it may debate a point long after winning it, leaving a partner more tired than persuaded.",
  "water-rooster": "Of all Roosters, the Water Rooster is usually considered the most communicative and intellectual. Publishing, policy analysis, translation, teaching and journalism are associated with it, as clarity and insight are rewarded in each. It enjoys organising ideas as much as objects, and it can explain a complicated subject so that everyone understands. In love, the Water Rooster is thoughtful, articulate and attentive, fond of long conversations over dinner. It needs intellectual companionship and someone who prizes candour. Over-analysis is its Achilles heel: it may dissect a partner's choices in detail or worry about small matters until a simple decision becomes complicated.",
  "wood-dog": "Warm, fair and cooperative, the Wood Dog is frequently called the conscience of a team. Social work, teaching, advocacy, human resources and charity management are commonly suggested, since a sense of justice and a talent for collaboration matter there. It works best when the mission is worthy and colleagues share its values. In love, the Wood Dog is loyal, generous and protective, always ready to answer the phone at any hour. Trust and integrity in a partner are non-negotiable for it. Overcommitment is the familiar danger here: it may take on too many people's troubles and become anxious or drained.",
  "fire-dog": "Champion of the underdog is the role tradition hands the Fire Dog. Activism, firefighting, employment law, campaigning journalism and youth coaching are frequently named, because courage and conviction carry real weight in each. It gives everything to a cause it believes in and expects colleagues to be straight with it; office spin or quiet favouritism can provoke a memorable outburst. In love the Fire Dog is ardent and loyal, the partner who will drive across the country at midnight if something goes wrong. Shared principles matter more to it than shared hobbies. Where things go awry is righteous anger: a perceived unfairness, even a small one, may ignite an argument out of all proportion to the original slight.",
  "earth-dog": "Steady, fair and practical, the Earth Dog is the dependable backbone many organisations quietly rely on. Facilities management, local government, insurance, school administration and trade associations suit it, since consistency and an honest word are valued there above sparkle. It likes knowing who is responsible for what and will cover a colleague's shift without fuss. Married or partnered, the Earth Dog tends to be patient and sensible, careful with shared money and attentive to elderly relatives and family traditions. It hopes for reliability returned in equal measure. The snag is a pessimistic streak: it may brace for the worst so habitually that a partner's excitement about a new plan meets a list of risks instead of enthusiasm.",
  "metal-dog": "The Metal Dog guards principles the way other signs guard property. Compliance, security, judicial administration, regulation and investigative work are typical callings, since a clear code and the nerve to enforce it are needed there. It is tireless once committed and openly uncomfortable with grey areas, so employers who state their values plainly earn its fierce dedication. In close bonds the Metal Dog is steadfast, honest and protective, the friend who never forgets a promise or a confidence. It asks for absolute trust and plain speaking. Clashes generally come from moral rigidity: it may treat a loved one's small white lie as a serious breach and find forgiveness slower than the other person would like.",
  "water-dog": "Perceptive and gentle, the Water Dog brings loyalty without the bark. Counselling, community nursing support, mediation, children's services and writing are commonly linked with it, as each rewards quiet empathy and an instinct for what people are not saying. It works best where kindness is not mistaken for weakness and where workloads stay humane. With loved ones the Water Dog is attentive, soft-spoken and deeply faithful, often the first to sense that a friend is struggling. It needs a partner who invites its opinions rather than assuming silence means agreement. The usual difficulty is anxiety turned inward: it may swallow its own needs to protect others, then grow quietly worried and withdrawn.",
  "wood-pig": "Generosity is almost a working method for the Wood Pig. Hospitality, community development, charity fundraising, food co-operatives and team-based creative work are frequently suggested, because goodwill and shared effort pay off there. It brings people together easily and tends to trust colleagues until given good reason not to. A sensible friend who reads the small print protects that trust. Behind the front door, the Wood Pig is affectionate, easy-going and happiest with a crowded table and a pot of something warming on the stove. It wants sincerity and someone who relishes a full house. Problems arise from over-giving: lending time, money or the spare room so freely that its own household feels stretched.",
  "fire-pig": "The Fire Pig brings appetite and enthusiasm to everything it touches. Restaurants, entertainment, sales, travel and festival management are typical arenas, as warmth and energy win customers there. It works hard in bursts, loves a team celebration and can talk a hesitant client round with genuine excitement. Over the long haul, though, it benefits from someone tracking the budget. In love the Fire Pig is passionate, demonstrative and generous to a fault, planning surprise feasts and weekend escapes. Honesty and plenty of affection keep it content. The recurring friction is indulgence: impulsive spending or a habit of saying yes to every invitation can strain a partner who prefers a quieter calendar.",
  "earth-pig": "Contentment through steady effort is the Earth Pig's hallmark. Catering, property management, retail ownership, agriculture and bookkeeping are commonly mentioned, since patience and a practical eye for comfort build value over time. It is a cheerful, reliable colleague who rarely seeks the limelight yet notices when the team needs feeding or a breather. In close relationships, the Earth Pig creates a warm, well-provisioned home and offers calm, unshowy devotion. It values security and a companion content with simple pleasures. The sore spot tends to be complacency: so comfortable with routine that necessary changes, from health habits to household plans, get postponed until a partner has to raise them repeatedly.",
  "metal-pig": "A Metal Pig keeps its good nature yet adds noticeable grit. Business ownership, law, construction management, wine and food trade and sports administration are typical fits, as sincerity backed by determination wins respect there. It pursues goals doggedly, says exactly what it thinks and will defend colleagues who are treated unfairly. Few people doubt where they stand with it. In love the Metal Pig is loyal, passionate and frank, giving its whole heart once it commits. It hopes for an equally direct partner who keeps their word. Tension tends to come from stubbornness and a long memory: once hurt, it may hold onto the grievance well after the other person believes it settled.",
  "water-pig": "Kindness and imagination shape the Water Pig's working life. Diplomacy, social services, the arts, hospitality and customer care suit it, because empathy and a knack for keeping the peace are valuable there. It tends to see the best in colleagues, smooths over tensions and quietly takes on extra work when someone is struggling. Firm deadlines and a candid manager help it turn goodwill into finished work. In close relationships the Water Pig is tender, forgiving and endlessly welcoming. It wants emotional sincerity and gentle handling. Friction usually arises from over-trust and avoidance: it may overlook warning signs, or postpone a needed conversation, because confrontation feels so much worse than mild discomfort.",
};
